    "body": "Pr #33223  adjusts the weight selection to keep the lighter coin when two coins have the same value, but the test has two mistakes\r\n\r\n1. It builds `mixed_weight_pool` but passes `utxo_pool` to `TestSRDSuccess`.\r\n2. There is nothing enforcing coin eviction because the current max weight (`4 * 3 * 67` = 804 WU) fits any two coins (544 WU)\r\n\r\nThe old existing test does not check the fix:\r\nIf you reverse #33223, it still passes 20/20 tests, which means it misses the tie-break\r\nOther coin selection tests like `spend_tests`, `wallet_send.py`, `wallet_fundrawtransaction.py` do not catch the broken tie-break\r\nThe fix\r\nThe PR uses `mixed_weight_pool` instead of `utxo_pool`.\r\nThe PR adds an extra light coin so that only two light coins can fit together and evicts a coin on every tie to pass.\r\nIt also lowers the max weight to `4 * 2 * (P2WPKH_INPUT_VSIZE - 1)` = 536 WU; SRD now has to evict the heavier coin on every tie to succeed\r\nAdds a second (67 vB) light coin to the pool\r\nThis should show 20/20 failed tests with [bitcoin#33223](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/33223) reverted and 20/20 passing without the revert\r\nSteps to reproduce:\r\nRevert the #33223  change in `src/wallet/coinselection.cpp`\r\n\r\n```\r\ngit show eff9e798b9 -- src/wallet/coinselection.cpp | git apply -R\r\n```\r\n\r\nBuild and run the tests\r\n\r\n```\r\ncmake --build build --target test_bitcoin\r\nbuild/bin/test_bitcoin --run_test=coinselection_tests/srd_test\r\n```\r\n\r\nExpected results: After the revert, it should fail on this PR and pass on master\r\n\r\ncc @yancyribbens",
